                        ],
                        "form": "whinged"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d70c7f6a-6f70-3150-b19f-0e3613f29579",
                        "entry_id": "f14ab6fa-af9b-3706-9b33-17986349f161",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To whine; to complain, especially in an annoying or persistent manner."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Commonwealth",
                            "Ireland",
                            "UK"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7572e279-dbe0-45d6-9143-9e49a06b74da",
                                "sense_id": "d70c7f6a-6f70-3150-b19f-0e3613f29579",
                                "text": "Argh! He has been whinging about it all night, even though he knows there's nothing we can do."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc287f6e-8028-4c33-881e-242ba76ca6a5",
                                "sense_id": "d70c7f6a-6f70-3150-b19f-0e3613f29579",
                                "text": "I know it won't help but sometimes it feels better to whinge about the things that annoy me."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c737d69-80a7-41c7-b0bb-d5b5b765de45",
                                "sense_id": "d70c7f6a-6f70-3150-b19f-0e3613f29579",
                                "text": "\"'D' ye hear what's come ower ye now,' continued the virago, 'ye whingeing Whig carles? D'ye hear wha's coming to cow yer cracks?\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "89c8bafb-249f-444b-ba2c-02e9695f9160",
                                "sense_id": "d70c7f6a-6f70-3150-b19f-0e3613f29579",
                                "text": "You crossed her last wish in death and yet you sulk with me because I don’t whinge like some hired mute from Lalouette’s."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "39462a1b-94de-46f2-b46f-ec18fe795e2b",
                                "sense_id": "d70c7f6a-6f70-3150-b19f-0e3613f29579",
                                "text": "Mostly, they were wingeing about the lousy cook and the same thing served too often"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b77fc1f-b329-4c5d-951e-5fc60a2d0b21",
                                "sense_id": "d70c7f6a-6f70-3150-b19f-0e3613f29579",
                                "text": "His wife will winge her bloody head off, but Nev will come good."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "affe8667-1aa2-421e-a648-78e9e7b9a682",
                                "sense_id": "d70c7f6a-6f70-3150-b19f-0e3613f29579",
                                "text": "“I try to write something that is amusing,” says [Kate] Spicer. “So much of the stuff written about sex is just whingeing, the I'm-not-getting-enough-orgasms kind of thing. It makes women sound as though they can't have fun in bed.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b8772b8f-100a-4e6d-aacb-10d863b69438",
                                "sense_id": "d70c7f6a-6f70-3150-b19f-0e3613f29579",
                                "text": "\"I'm miserable,\" Sam proclaimed, plodding behind with his shoelace flapping. \"Nobody ever gives me butter-pies when I need them.\" / \"Shut up,\" said Jonathan. \"Stop wingeing.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "53dde5e0-8c1f-457a-8c09-f4fdc07ff422",
                                "sense_id": "d70c7f6a-6f70-3150-b19f-0e3613f29579",
                                "text": "\"You know the problem these days with young people? Get them to carry a 500-pound bomb and within 30 seconds they're making noises,\" he says, imitating a whingeing sound."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
